SUPER_COL STATUS:
- quantity: we need any with numbers that aren't dates or variants, but it might actually be the case that all numbers in this column are actually quantity (even if they are in the format "Frigates (5 + 1)"). We also need to identify any other quantity-like columns, and differentiate them from non-quantities (particularly difficult case: raw_cols "no." or "number" might be a quantity or serial number, and map to quantity or other_names respectively; there may be some other "qty-look-alikes")
- origin super_cols (origin, cost, dates, status): not vital right now. Will be useful when deduplicating for a master equipment list later. Only assign if they are un-ambiguous
- mission cols (role, capability, propulsion): same as sub_class & quantity: add other_classes to the appropriate columns, and combine with any obvious raw_cols
- equip_type: vital. I'm not sure how to tease that out right now from ambiguous raw_col names
- other type cols (other_names, variant, ship_name): sort if obvious, set aside for disambiguation with equip_type. eventually, variant will take on the old equip_types as that is deduplicated in Phase IV

name/origin, etc.

